// `then calls NAME:(...)` (args/) or `then calls NAME:[N]` (count.id), and
// what the `:(...)` form needs from outside its own block: one recorded row
// written the way the clause writes it, for a miss to show
// (args/cmp.id), and the list types among NAME's parameters, noted with
// the ones cases compare at (ctype/list/note/from/then.id) -- the row condition
// compares those columns with idtc_eq_K and the miss prints them with
// idtc_show_K, and neither exists for a type nothing else noted.

emit_then_calls(int ci, int ti, int node) {
  string kind = k_of(node);
  if(kind == "thencalls") {
    emit_calls_args(ci, ti, node);
  } else {
    emit_calls_count(ci, ti, node);
  }
} return void;
